---
/* Where each of these Falco came from, and where each of them went.

   The figure itself is the kit's now — Defranceski draws five families
   arriving in Istria from five directions, this archive was asked to match
   that grammar, and Luwinski hand-rolled the same lanes for the same reason.
   What stays here is the only part that was ever this archive's: the bands,
   which used to be a forty-line JavaScript array in this file and are
   src/data/strands.json now, because a list only a template can reach cannot
   be counted, checked or added to.

   WHY THIS ARCHIVE'S FIGURE IS THE OTHER WAY ROUND. The de Franceschi strands
   are five families arriving from five directions. The Falco problem is the
   opposite shape: ONE line that stays put for seven generations and then
   crosses the world in a single lifetime, and FOUR other groups of the
   surname this archive can name and cannot join to it. So the first band is
   the line and the rest are the strands it is not.

   THE FOUR HOUSEHOLDS ON STRADA CAMELLARA ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. They
   never move, and a figure about where people came from would have to invent
   a journey for them. They are drawn on /lines, in the band that exists to
   say «these do not connect».

   EVERY NODE IS A DOCUMENT. Nothing in this figure is inferred, and the
   numbers in the last band are counts of harvested rows, not of people. */
import Strands from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/Strands.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import data from "../data/strands.json";
---
<Strands bands={data.bands} title={data.title} alt={data.alt} u={u} />
